r. Geom. Topol. 8 (2008) 1763-1780.\n\n  * (with M.Ottina) A geometric decomposition of spaces into cells of different types II : Homology theory. Topology Appl. 155 (2008) 1777-1785.\n\n  * (with J. Barmak) Simple homotopy types and finite spaces. Adv. Math. 218 (2008) 87-104.\n\n  * (with J.Barmak) Minimal finite models. J. Homotopy Relat. Struct. 2 (2007) 127-140.\n\n  * (with M.del Hoyo) Classical invariants for global actions and groupoid atlases. Appl. Categ. Struct. 16 (2008) 689-721.\n\n  * (with J.Barmak) 2-Dimension from the Topological Viewpoint. Order 24 (2007) 49-58.\n\n  * (with M.Ottina) A Geometric Decomposition of Spaces into Cells of Different Types. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOne-point reductions of finite spaces, h-regular CW-complexes and collapsibility (https://arxiv.org/abs/0801.0007)\nciteturn4academia17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 18.9 years ago; Authors: Jonathan Ariel Barmak, Elias Gabriel Minian ... These methods allow one to study homotopy theory of cell complexes by means of elementary moves of their finite models.\nTitle: One-point reductions of finite spaces, h-regular CW-complexes and collapsibility\nAuthors: Jonathan Ariel Barmak, Elias Gabriel Minian\nDate: Fri Dec 28 21:23:51 2007\n\nWe investigate one-point reduction methods of finite topological spaces. These methods allow one to study homotopy theory of cell complexes by means of elementary moves of their finite models. We also introduce the notion of h-regular CW-complex, generalizing the concept of regular CW-complex, and prove that the h-regular CW-complexes, which are a sort of combinatorial-up-to-homotopy objects, are modeled (up to homotopy) by their associated finite spaces. This is accomplished by generalizing a classical result of McCord on simplicial complexes.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nΑποτελέσματα αναζήτησης - \"Equivariant PL-topology\" :: Library Catalog 